WEBVTT

00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:14,380
Should I eat gluten-free sourdough bread with a cancer history?

00:00:14,380 --> 00:00:19,120
And I've considered making my own sense there's so many ingredients of the store-bought

00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:24,620
brands which I purchase regularly.

00:00:24,620 --> 00:00:33,460
Um, okay, so, first of all, gluten is gluten-good for cancer.

00:00:34,020 --> 00:00:42,820
Well, gluten typically is not a direct feeder of cancer, so it's not going to be a fuel source

00:00:42,820 --> 00:00:48,500
of cancer. So some people will say, I stopped eating gluten because of my cancer.

00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:54,340
Well, there can be a lot of good things in that statement, but gluten is typically not going

00:00:54,340 --> 00:01:02,180
to be a direct fuel source for cancer. Other than why should, or should a cancer patient stop

00:01:02,180 --> 00:01:10,740
eating gluten? Well, the benefit of stop of limiting gluten is that gluten is so pro-inflammatory.

00:01:11,220 --> 00:01:16,900
So remember, we're trying to kill cancer cells. We don't need to be, you know,

00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:25,220
splitting our army to fight different things. And if we are eating an inflammatory diet, which gluten

00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:31,780
would be, you know, number one on that inflammation list and then bad oils and things like that would

00:01:31,780 --> 00:01:39,380
be in that category as well. But if we're causing more inflammation in our gut and in our brain,

00:01:39,380 --> 00:01:46,980
it's going to be more difficult to fight cancer and kill cancer cells. So you want to, you know,

00:01:46,980 --> 00:01:54,660
clean up your diet as best as possible so that your body can focus on what you want it to focus on. So

00:01:55,460 --> 00:02:05,460
that being said, going gluten-free as a cancer patient has its benefits. Going gluten-free,

00:02:06,100 --> 00:02:12,820
even if you don't have cancer has its benefits. Same reasons I just gave. So gluten is so inflammatory.

00:02:15,380 --> 00:02:22,660
But in that understanding, if I'm going to start eating gluten-free foods, you're often going to

00:02:22,660 --> 00:02:30,740
get foods that are not organic. And then you're going to get foods like this question says

00:02:30,740 --> 00:02:35,860
that you're going to get foods that have a lot of different ingredients that you don't want to be

00:02:35,860 --> 00:02:43,540
eating. So that is an issue as well. So you have to balance it out. What would be the best thing

00:02:43,540 --> 00:02:48,020
to do? Well, the best thing to do would be to make your own bread if you want to eat bread.

00:02:48,100 --> 00:02:57,300
And the other part of this question, sourdough bread has its own benefits. So many people who

00:02:57,860 --> 00:03:04,820
are not cancer patients and are eating a gluten-free diet find that they can eat gluten-free sourdough

00:03:04,820 --> 00:03:11,220
bread with very little problem or much less problem than if they eat regular gluten bread.

00:03:12,180 --> 00:03:20,420
And they switch over from a gluten-free product to a sourdough bread. But if you're going to

00:03:20,420 --> 00:03:29,220
start making your own, you could make your own out of a clean gluten-free flower. And then you're

00:03:29,220 --> 00:03:37,540
solving both problems. You're not getting the gluten at all. And you're using a clean flower

00:03:37,700 --> 00:03:44,180
organic flower, if you can find it, an organic gluten-free flower. Best thing would be to make your own

00:03:44,180 --> 00:03:51,300
flower with organic materials that's gluten-free. And then make your own sourdough, start with your

00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:57,860
own culture and make your own sourdough bread. Now, you know, obviously it sounds like you have

00:03:57,860 --> 00:04:03,380
the ability to do that. Now, the negative issue of making your own sourdough is that you're committed

00:04:03,380 --> 00:04:09,620
to making bread almost every day. And unless you're making it as a ministry and giving it away.

00:04:11,060 --> 00:04:18,340
But it can be overwhelming for people, for the law law. Now, you can make it every day for two

00:04:18,340 --> 00:04:25,060
months and freeze it. And that's another solution that you could go off and not make it for three months.

00:04:25,060 --> 00:04:30,660
So there's different things that you could do. But yes, can you make your own gluten-free sourdough

00:04:31,620 --> 00:04:37,940
would that be good for a person with cancer? Well, it's certainly a great option. You're not getting

00:04:37,940 --> 00:04:46,580
the gluten and you're getting the benefits of sourdough. So I would say, yes, go for it. Stay gluten-free,

00:04:47,300 --> 00:04:53,540
isn't always on everybody's list. But on everybody's list, I put limit gluten because gluten is so

00:04:53,540 --> 00:05:02,660
inflammatory. So that would be the last suggestion.

